Vulkan engine: consecutive draws share a render pass, released textures/views die after the batch, presents read back only when dumped (MAGI-5)

Drain profile mg5-p2/mg5-vw1 (Survival tutorial street): the FIFO thread waited on GPU fences ~390 ms per second.
1. vk_eng_draw continues the open render pass while the next draw targets the same framebuffer and area
   (was: begin + end, i.e. LOAD/STORE of every attachment, plus a full barrier, per draw; ~4900 draws/s ->
   ~460 passes/s). Anything else recorded (vk_rec_begin) and every flush ends the pass first.
   PS3RECOMP_VK_PASS_MERGE=0 = one pass per draw.
2. vk_eng_release: a texture or view released while the batch is open is destroyed after the batch's
   submit-and-wait (graveyard emptied in vk_batch_flush) instead of flushing first (~20% of the drain:
   texture-cache replacement mid-frame). Colour/depth targets unchanged.
3. vk_cb_present: on the engine path the full-frame readback + submit-and-wait runs only on presents that
   are dumped (nothing else reads them; rsx_vulkan_backend_readback_center asks the engine). This one was
   waiting for every frame's whole render: fence wait 380 -> 127 ms/s (mg5-st1).
4. VK_WAIT_STATS=1 (diag): fence-wait ms, submits, draws, passes per second and a wait-length histogram.
Reviewed by MAGI-6 (graveyard emptied at shutdown, per review).

